(globalThis.CATALOGUE_RECORD_CHUNKS??=Object.create(null))[532]={"source_order":532,"notes":["The faint grey marks across the page were judged to be show-through from fol. 266 recto, based on its mirrored layout matching that page. It is possible, though unlikely, that some very faint pencil writing is hidden among them. No independent target-page writing was discernible at native resolution.","The strip right of the gutter, at about x>3200, belongs to the facing page (fol. 267). It shows a circled 'ta…' and an 'f.' near the top, and a column of shelfmark letters 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'e.', 'd'. These are facing-page fragments and are not recorded as target blocks.","The lower portion of the leaf, below about y≈3240, appears to be a separate or folded paper layer whose edge is visible. Its ruled lines continue, and it carries no writing.","Image review at native resolution of all tiles found no catalogue text on fol. 266b apart from the folio number. The top, middle, bottom, outer margin, gutter and interlinear spaces were all checked.","Very faint mirrored grey traces across the ruled area are show-through from the recto, fol. 266. They are not transcribed as text of this page.","Physical features with no writing: a dark notch or tab at the top edge at about x 730–800. A horizontal edge of an overlapping or folded paper layer at about y 3230–3270. Binding thread in the gutter at about x 3150–3200. Scattered paper specks.","The strip to the right of the gutter, at about x>3200, belongs to the facing page, fol. 267. It shows a circled 'ta…', 'f.', and a column of 'd.', 'e.' shelfmark letters. These are facing-page fragments and are not recorded here.","There is a horizontal paper edge at about y≈3230–3270, running across the full width. The adjacent fol. 266 has a shorter native height (3595) than this canvas (5120). This suggests the upper part of the canvas may be the verso of a shorter leaf, with the area below the edge belonging to an underlying leaf. It is not resolved whether the ruled area below y≈3270 belongs to fol. 266b or to another leaf. That area carries only faint show-through and no legible writing.","The facing strip at about x>3200 has several marks: a circled 'ta…', 'f.…', and a column 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'e.', followed by further partial letters ('d', 'd/a', 'c') lower down. This column does not obviously match the shelfmark column visible in the left margin of the fol. 267 overview (c. 343, d. 706, c. 242 …). It may belong to an intervening leaf or slip rather than fol. 267. Its identity is left unresolved, and it is not a target-page record.","Faint grey mirrored traces across the ruled area are judged to be show-through. It cannot be fully excluded that very faint independent pencil writing is hidden among them."],"records":[{"id":"css-prod-0532-r001","local_id":"r001","source_order":532,"folio":"266b","folio_label":"fol. 266b","sequence":1,"page_id":"1f04d864-0c53-407a-bd7c-a471e8a7a390","kind":"other","record_type":"non_catalogue_text","source_model_record_type":"non_catalogue_text","subtype":"folio_number","shelfmark":"","titleLiteral":"","titleNormalized":"","displayTitle":"Catalogue text","authorOrSource":"","source":"","subject":"","subjectGroup":"","date":"","extent":"","lines":"","script":"","incipit":"","transcription":"266b.","annotations":["Pencil folio number in the top-left corner of the leaf, at about [330,300,140,170].","The 'b' is written superscript after '266', with a dot beneath or after it."],"uncertainties":["The mark after the superscript b is read as a dot or full stop. Its exact form is uncertain.","There is a horizontal paper edge at about y≈3230–3270, running across the full width. The adjacent fol. 266 has a shorter native height (3595) than this canvas (5120). This suggests the upper part of the canvas may be the verso of a shorter leaf, with the area below the edge belonging to an underlying leaf. It is not resolved whether the ruled area below y≈3270 belongs to fol. 266b or to another leaf. That area carries only faint show-through and no legible writing.","The facing strip at about x>3200 has several marks: a circled 'ta…', 'f.…', and a column 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'd.', 'e.', followed by further partial letters ('d', 'd/a', 'c') lower down. This column does not obviously match the shelfmark column visible in the left margin of the fol. 267 overview (c. 343, d. 706, c. 242 …). It may belong to an intervening leaf or slip rather than fol. 267. Its identity is left unresolved, and it is not a target-page record.","Faint grey mirrored traces across the ruled area are judged to be show-through. It cannot be fully excluded that very faint independent pencil writing is hidden among them."],"focused_readings":[],"reviewNotes":[],"editorialNotes":[],"relationships":[],"editorial_context":[],"block_ids":["b001"],"locations":[{"block_id":"b001","bbox":[330,300,140,170]}],"isCancelled":false,"needsReview":true,"human_verified":false,"verification_status":"machine_reviewed","change_audit":[],"sourceCitationURL":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/canvas/1f04d864-0c53-407a-bd7c-a471e8a7a390.json","auditPath":"audit/pages/0532.json","attachedNotes":[],"resolvedRelationships":[],"attachedRecords":[]}]};
